WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.820
Welcome to another
Stories From The Stores

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.180
We're joined today by curator Sarah Bond and she's told me that both these objects

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:14.080
were used to detect pregnancy in the last hundred years. Sarah, how is this true?

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.640
Both of them are used to detect a hormone in pregnant woman's urine called HCG.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.800
Scientists first discovered this hormone in the 1920s.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.780
HCG is really important in preserving the pregnancy,

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.780
in the very early stages before the placenta takes over

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.700
and when you introduce most animals to this hormone they will ovulate.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:39.900
So the same scientists that discovered HCG found that if you injected it into immature female mice and rabbits

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.340
they would start to ovulate and their sexual organs would mature,

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.280
but the were expensive and they took quite a long time.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:52.480
Just one pregnancy test required five separate mice and all of them had to be dissected at the end of the process.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:58.380
So by the 1930s scientists were wondering could you use an animal that didn't need to be dissected?

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:02.640
These are a species of Japanese Bitterling, a tropical fish

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.830
and as you can probably see they've got
quite translucent skins. The fish have

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:12.800
an organ that they used to produce eggs
and that organ expands in the presence of HCG

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:17.880
and so you can see how this works.
This first one here - its organ which is

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:22.300
called an ovipositor - is quite a bit
longer than the second one which is a normal fish

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:26.760
and the last one here is just been dissected to show that organ a little bit more clearly

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.100
but essentially that organ would go all the way from about 2mm up to about 25mm.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.280
Was it super accurate?

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.700
No not quite, unfortunately that was the
sticking point with this test.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:41.560
They weren't very accurate and even men's urine could often produce a positive result.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:46.120
So just a few years after the fish, a British zoologist working in South Africa

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:52.420
found that if you injected a particular type of frog with pregnant women's urine

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.580
it would spontaneously lay eggs, what's more it would do so within 12 hours.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.920
So if the animals are so good, why did it take so long to get to this?

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:06.180
Well in fact the frog test, as it became known, was used up until the late 1960s and early 1970s

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.120
and it absolutely was the standard pregnancy test all over the world.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:10.979
There was a lot of drive to develop a test

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:15.810
that women could take in their own homes, just like this one which is an early

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:18.900
home pregnancy test kit. They are still detecting exactly the same hormone

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.680
it works from a different process, it's a chemical
process so no animals are involved.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.940
So if the frogs took 12 hours, how long does this take?

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.700
The very first chemical pregnancy
test took around 2 hours, which was still

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:34.290
a vast improvement and now you can find
out the result in a matter of minutes.

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:38.320
So if the animal test was so good would you still feel comfortable going back to the fish today?

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.750
The fish not so much because
they were so unreliable, if the frog tests

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:46.260
were still around and it was the
only option I had then sure, but at the

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:49.080
end of the day it was so much easier
just to be able to walk into a chemist

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:54.820
pick up a test like this, take it home and then I was the first person to find out I was pregnant.

